# Citation metadata for SPECTRA.
#
# This describes an UNRELEASED WORK IN PROGRESS. There is no release, no tag and
# no archived artifact, so this file deliberately carries:
#   - no `version`        (nothing has been versioned)
#   - no `date-released`  (nothing has been released)
#   - no `doi` / `identifiers` (nothing has been deposited or archived)
# Add those fields in the same commit that creates the first tag, and not before.
#
# TODO(decision: citation-author) The author entry records a given name only,
# because the citable form of the author's name has not been confirmed. Add
# `family-names:` and, if one exists, `orcid:` before the first release.
# TODO(decision: repo-url) github.com/rakshit-737/spectra-security is a placeholder path.
# Change it here, in CONTRIBUTING.md, in CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md and in the Go module
# path together.

cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  SPECTRA is an unreleased work in progress. If you refer to it, please cite the
  repository and the commit SHA you looked at; there is no release, no DOI and no
  published result to cite yet.
title: "SPECTRA: Security State Reconstruction, Causal Analysis and Attack Replay"
type: software
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/rakshit-737/spectra-security"
abstract: >-
  A deterministic, offline, local-first research platform that reconstructs
  security state from synthetic telemetry, emits evidence-licensed cut proofs
  over a declared control catalog, and replays scenarios under alternative
  control configurations. It proves properties of its own model -- a hand-written
  rule table, an entity resolution pass, a declared control catalog and the
  telemetry actually ingested -- and not properties of any real system. Work in
  progress: no component is complete and no result has been measured.
keywords:
  - security-state
  - causal-analysis
  - attack-replay
  - minimal-cut
  - provenance
  - reproducible-research
  - offline-first
authors:
  - given-names: Rakshit
  # Claude is listed because it generated the substance of this repository, not
  # merely as a tool acknowledgement. The specification text, the planning
  # documents, the conflict audit and the skeleton files were written by Claude
  # under direction. Direction, scope, decisions and review are the human
  # author's. Listing it as an author is the honest description of how the work
  # was produced; omitting it would not be.
  - name: "Claude (Anthropic)"
    website: "https://claude.com/claude-code"
